REM Ragnar Rubber Ducky - built-in demo / validation script.
REM
REM SAFE: this script only TYPES text. It runs no commands and uses no
REM Run/terminal shortcuts, so it cannot change the target host.
REM
REM How to validate:
REM   1) Plug the Pi into the target host's USB port.
REM   2) On that host, click into any text field (Notepad, a browser search
REM      box, a chat box - anything that shows typed characters).
REM   3) Back in Ragnar: Pentest tab > Rubber Ducky > pick this script,
REM      pick the /dev/hidg0 target, press Execute.
REM   4) Watch the text below appear in the focused field.

DELAY 1500
STRING Ragnar Rubber Ducky OK
ENTER
STRING Shift check: Hello, World! 1234567890 !?@#_+
ENTER
STRING If you can read these two lines, HID keystroke injection works.
